# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Item 738: a captured Structure used whole (`probe(loc)`). The reader keeps
# the copy the host made; probe is admitted the whole Structure and reads its
# value field: 40 + 2. The norm does not forbid the whole use; the earlier
# refusal pinned an implementation limit. Entry 7.
Model:
    int: other 5
    box:
        int: c 5
    int: count 0
    int: value 0
end: Model

fn: probe (Model: q) int
    return: q\value

fn: makeReader (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    loc: merge Model
    loc\value: n
    fn: read (int: x) int
        return: probe(loc) + x
    return: read

@: r40 makeReader(40)
int: a (r40: 2)
int: ok 7
if: a != 42
    ok: 1
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
